      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since the MySQL connection is unavailable (persistent authentication error `1045`), I'll finalize the query based on the semantic network evidence and prior metric SQL. Below is the investigation report.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (investigated):**\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — Dimension for academic departments: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (e.g., 'Mathematics'), `DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME`, `SCHOOL_CODE/NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` ('Y'/'N'), `DEPT_BUDGET_CODE`. Granularity: one row per department. The only table that has the degree-granting flag.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — Subject-level rollup per term: `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `SUBJECT_TITLE`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (number of students enrolled in the subject), `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER`, unit counts. Granularity: one row per subject per term.\n- **SUBJECT_SUMMARY** — Subject-level final enrollment statistics per term: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` (official registrar enrollment), weekly/credit/listener breakdowns.\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Catalog-level subject offerings per academic year/term: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `SUBJECT_TITLE`, `SUBJECT_SHORT_TITLE`, unit counts, HGN, offering flags. This is the \"course catalog.\"\n- **CIS_COURSE_CATALOG / DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG** — Alternative catalog feeds with the same subject attribute structure (via `concept_course_catalog_sources`).\n- **STUDENT_DEPARTMENT** — Lightweight department lookup (no degree-granting flag).\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Program-scope enrollment snapshots (textbook / library reserve scope only).\n\n**Column concepts:**\n- **column_concept_enrollment_measures** — Distinguishes `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (headcount) from `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` (official registrar enrollment). Decision guide: \"For questions about the number of enrolled students per subject offering or **department-level totals**: use NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS from SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject granularity).\"\n- **column_concept_department_name** — Contrast between DEPARTMENT_NAME and OFFER_DEPT_NAME conventions; same academic value domain.\n\n**Concepts:**\n- **concept_department_dimension** — Decision guide: \"For questions filtering departments by degree-granting status: use SIS_DEPARTMENT; it has … IS_DEGREE_GRANTING.\"\n- **concept_subject_offering_facts**, **concept_course_catalog_sources** — Group the fact/catalog tables above.\n\n**Prior metrics:**\n- **dw_1288** — Uses exactly the \"total enrolled students exceeds the average across all departments by more than one standard deviation (STDDEV)\" pattern: per-department `SUM(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` totals, then `HAVING total > (SELECT AVG(t) + STDDEV(t) FROM (per-department totals))`, restricted to Mathematics (code '18').\n- **dw_1335** — UNION ALL of two branches with a literal \"reason for inclusion\" column and NULLs for branch-specific measures.\n- **dw_4387 / dw_3868** — Department totals vs. average-total-enrollment comparisons.\n- **dw_1302** — Degree-granting departments excluding `'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'` (the exact spelling of the department name in the data).\n\n### 2. Lineage and Relationships\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY joins → SIS_DEPARTMENT (`OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE`), SUBJECT_OFFERED (child at section granularity), SUBJECT_SUMMARY (via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY), COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (via SUBJECT_ID/TERM_CODE).\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED joins → SIS_DEPARTMENT (`DEPARTMENT_CODE`), ACADEMIC_TERMS, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT is the hub of the department dimension; per `concept_department_dimension`, it is the canonical source for `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`.\n\n### 3. Differences Between Similar Entities\n\n**3a. Enrollment measure candidates for \"total enrolled students across all subjects offered by that department\":**\n\n| Dimension | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER | TIP/LIBRARY NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Meaning | Student headcount, subject granularity (column_concept_enrollment_measures) | Official registrar final enrollment | Program-scope snapshot |\n| Coverage | All subjects offered (registrar) | All subjects per term | Textbook/library scope only — \"may not cover all subjects\" (documented caveat) |\n| Department totals | Explicitly recommended in decision_guide for \"department totals\" | Recommended for \"official subject enrollment\" filters | Used in dw_1288, but that question explicitly says \"library and tip subject offerings\" |\n\n**3b. Fitness to task requirements:**\n- Requirement: \"total enrolled students across all subjects offered by that department\" → SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS: supported (decision_guide verbatim match). TIP/LIBRARY: violation (question does not limit to those programs). SUBJECT_SUMMARY: possible, but the wording \"enrolled students\" lexically matches NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, and dw_1288's identical \"> AVG + STDDEV\" pattern uses the SUM of NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS.\n- Requirement: \"degree-granting\" → only SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING: supported.\n- Requirement: \"courses listed in the course catalog\" + \"distinct course titles\" → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE: supported (the table is literally named course catalog and has SUBJECT_TITLE).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-field anchoring:** \"course catalog\" → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (primary warehouse catalog; CIS/Drupal are alternative feeds — the warehouse table is the canonical \"course catalog\" in prior cases like dw_4387). \"distinct course titles\" → COUNT(DISTINCT SUBJECT_TITLE). \"Electrical Engineering and Computer Science\" → `DEPARTMENT_NAME != 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'` (spelling per dw_1302).\n\n**3d. Evidence from prior cases:** \"> mean + STDDEV across departments\" pattern: 1 prior case (dw_1288, using SUM(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) per department). UNION-with-reason pattern: 1 prior case (dw_1335). Degree-granting filter excluding EECS: dw_1302, dw_1474.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nSIS_DEPARTMENT is used in nearly all department-scoped metrics for degree-granting/school filtering. SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY provides department-level enrollment totals (dw_1335, dw_4683). COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED provides catalog attributes and titles (dw_4387, dw_2151).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nInvestigated: SIS_DEPARTMENT, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (semantic_get / semantic_search descriptions); concepts concept_department_dimension, concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_course_catalog_sources (semantic_get/graph); column_concept_enrollment_measures, column_concept_department_name (semantic_get/graph); metrics dw_1288, dw_1335, dw_4387, dw_3868, dw_1302, dw_3163 (semantic_get with full SQL). Graph traversals: query_neighbors on SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY and COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED. mysql_query was attempted 8 times; all failed with access denied (1045), so data-level verification was not possible — noted explicitly.\n\n### 6. Recommendations\n\n**6a.** Use SIS_DEPARTMENT (code, name, IS_DEGREE_GRANTING), SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (SUM of NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS per OFFER_DEPT_CODE), COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (COUNT(DISTINCT SUBJECT_TITLE)).\n\n**6b.** Two CTE branches joined by UNION ALL (prior case dw_1335): Branch 1 computes per-department enrollment totals, filters to Mathematics whose total exceeds AVG + STDDEV of all-department totals (prior case dw_1288), and outputs the total with NULL course title count. Branch 2 joins SIS_DEPARTMENT (IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y', name ≠ 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci') to the catalog, groups by department, HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT SUBJECT_TITLE) >= 5, and outputs the title count with NULL enrollment. No rounding anywhere.\n\n**6c.** *Data*: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY is at subject granularity with NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS — summing per department gives department totals without fanout; COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED joins 1:1 to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT_CODE. *Semantic network*: enrollment decision_guide prescribes NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS for department totals; department concept guide prescribes SIS_DEPARTMENT for degree-granting. *Business*: dw_1288 is a prior case of the identical statistical filter; dw_1335 is a prior case of the identical output shape.\n\n**6d.** Alternative: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER could also be used for \"enrolled students\"; the tiebreaker is the decision_guide wording (\"department totals\" → NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) and dw_1288's prior case, both of which support the chosen column.\n\n",
